<<<
super-. The use of this as an abbreviation for ‘of a superior kind ’, as in superman, super-Dreadnought, supercritic, & scores or hundreds of other words, is so evidently convenient that it is vain to protest when others indulge in it, & so evidently barbarous that it is worth while to circumvent it oneself when one can do so without becoming unintelligible.
===
**super-.** The use of this as an abbreviation for 'of a superior kind', as in *superman, super-Dreadnought, supercritic,* & scores or hundreds of other words, is so evidently convenient that it is vain to protest when others indulge in it, & so evidently barbarous that it is worth while to circumvent it oneself when one can do so without becoming unintelligible.
>>>

<<<
Super-cinema, meaning merely a cinema of exceptional size or splendour, & not something that transcends & thereby ceases to be a cinema, may serve as a specimen of the worse applications.
===
*Super-cinema,* meaning merely a cinema of exceptional size or splendour, & not something that transcends & thereby ceases to be a cinema, may serve as a specimen of the worse applications.
>>>

